15 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Workflow diagram for federated learning-based disease classification using the Mendeley dataset, detailing data preparation, augmentation, client partitioning, model training using FedAvg with six deep learning architectures, ONNX export, API deployment, Docker container use, Hugging Face Spaces deployment, and real-time inference steps.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Panel \(a\) shows a pomegranate fruit with dark sunken lesions caused by Alternaria. Panel \(b\) displays a fruit with large irregular black spots from Anthracnose. Panel \(c\) depicts a fruit with severe cracking and rot due to bacterial blight. Panel \(d\) presents a pomegranate with brownish speckling and discoloration from Cercospora. Panel \(e\) demonstrates a healthy pomegranate with smooth unblemished red skin.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Six confusion matrices compare performance of CNN, ResNet50, ConvNeXt_V2, EfficientNetV2, MobileViT, and ViT-B models for classifying five plant disease categories: Alternaria, Anthracnose, Bacterial Blight, Cercospora, and Healthy. Each matrix shows predicted versus true classes with cell counts, highlighting strong classification performance, especially for the Healthy class.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Four-panel graphic showing the process for pomegranate disease detection using a web application. The first panel displays the web address, the second is the application interface, the third shows a person using a smartphone to scan pomegranates, and the fourth presents the healthy diagnosis result on the app screen.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Grid of five pomegranate images in the top row labeled \215Original Images,\216 followed by six rows showing heatmap visualizations labeled CNN, ResNet50, ConvNeXt V2, EfficientNetV2, MobileViT, and ViT-B, each row corresponding to a different deep learning model\220s focus on different parts of the fruit for defect detection.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
